ucceed in getting their  hands on the new proceeds on the new  profits  the fear of marijuana activists is that  the law will actually  only help international corporations get  into the mexican market  and sell to richer urban consumers while  elsewhere the street corner business  continues as normal  but in a socially conservative country  where any talk of drug legalization is  deeply controversial  both senators and advocates hope this  could be the start of change  john holman al jazeera mexico city
 

